  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZCC Amplifying the prophetic voice: Enhancing access to basic health services, sexual and reproductive health and rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will leverage on the role of the church to address the problems described in the section above. Access to health is a social justice issue. Research has shown that Christian mission hospitals and health programs account for about 50% of all healthcare&#xa0; delivered in Sub-Saharan Africa (Olivier et al. 2015). Churches are subsystems of communities and have been instrumental in the delivery of health services in Zimbabwe. This work is in line with the purpose of the church, which is worship, teaching, fellowship, evangelizing and serving humanity. ZCC will therefore strength the role of the church in improving access to basic health care and SRHR services in targeted communities. The ZCC has an existing Health structure, at Secretariat level it has the Health Desk coordinated by the Health Coordinator. Within communities the ZCC has existing Ecumenical Health Champions who have been instrumental in reaching out to communities with health awareness since 2019. The ZCC has also an existing Health Commission which has the mandate to improve service provision standards and coordination mechanisms by mission health care facilities as well as spearhead high-level policy advocacy and ecumenical executive accompaniment on health.
Objectives
1.&#xa0; To improve SRH knowledge, attitude and practices among adolescent boys and girls and young men and women in targeted communities
2. To increase access to youth and disability friendly SRH services
3.To empower women and girls to take control of their menstrual health and SRH</narrative>
  </description>
